---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="Terms for using the Orso marketing website. The studio itself is open source — see the project license for the software."
>
  <article class="shell py-section sm:py-section-wide">
    <p class="text-eyebrow uppercase text-faint">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-h2 tracking-tight text-balance">Terms</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-label text-faint">Last updated: 6 November 2026</p>
    <div class="prose mt-10 max-w-2xl dark:prose-invert">
      <p>
        These terms apply to this marketing website. The Orso application and related source code
        are governed by the license in
        <a href="https://github.com/Blaise1030/cms/blob/main/LICENSE">the project repository</a>,
        not by this page.
      </p>
      <h2>Using this site</h2>
      <p>
        You may browse these pages for information about Orso. Do not attempt to disrupt the site,
        scrape it in a way that harms availability, or present the content as your own product.
      </p>
      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided as-is for information. Product details may change; always check the
        repository and app for the current behaviour. Nothing here is legal, financial, or
        professional advice.
      </p>
      <h2>Your sites and content</h2>
      <p>
        Sites you build or edit with Orso remain yours. Publishing, hosting, and third-party agent
        terms (Claude, Cursor, Codex, GitHub, and so on) are between you and those providers.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: open an issue on
        <a href="https://github.com/Blaise1030/cms">the Orso repository</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
